---`Rects` are used to represent an X and Y position with accompanying width and height dimensions.
---
---Info: The X and Y positions are the Left and Top of the rectangle respectively.
---@class Rect
---@field x number (Writeable) The X position of the rectangle.
---@field y number (Writeable) The Y position of the rectangle.
---@field width number (Writeable) The width of the rectangle.
---@field height number (Writeable) The height of the rectangle.
---@field left number (Writeable) The left edge of the rectangle. `left = x`
---@field top number (Writeable) The upper edge of the rectangle. `top = y`
---@field right number (Writeable) The right edge of the rectangle. `right = x + width`
---@field bottom number (Writeable) The lower edge of the rectangle. `bottom = y + height`
---@field centreX number (Read-only) The X position of the centre point of the rectangle. `centreX = x + (width / 2)`
---@field centreY number (Read-only) The Y position of the centre point of the rectangle. `centreY = y + (height / 2)`
Rect = {}

---Creates and returns a rectangle with the provided values, or with all elements set to 0 if no arguments were
---provided.
---@return Rect # The newly created rectangle
---@overload fun(x: number, y: number, width: number, height: number): Rect
function Rect.new() end

---Moves the rectangle's X and Y elements by the given input values.
---@param offsetX number The offset applied to the X element.
---@param offsetY number The offset applied to the Y element.
function Rect:Translate(offsetX, offsetY) end

---Increases each edge of the rectangle by the given horizontal and vertical values.
---
---Info: The calculation for this method is:
---@param horizontal number The expansion applied to the left and right edges of the rectangle.
---@param vertical number The expansion applied to the top and bottom edges of the rectangle.
function Rect:Grow(horizontal, vertical) end

---Decreases each edge of the rectangle by the given horizontal and vertical values.
---
---Info: The calculation for this method is:
---@param horizontal number The reduction applied to the left and right edges of the rectangle.
---@param vertical number The reduction applied to the top and bottom edges of the rectangle.
function Rect:Shrink(horizontal, vertical) end

---Scales the rectangle about 0,0 by the given amount.
---
---Info: The calculation for this method is:
---@param scale number The scaling value to apply to all elements in the rectangle.
function Rect:Scale(scale) end

---Returns whether the given X and Y position is within this rectangle
---@param x number The X position to test.
---@param y number The Y position to test.
---@return boolean # Whether the given position is within this rectangle.
---@overload fun(self: Rect, rect: Rect): boolean
function Rect:Contains(x, y) end

---Returns whether the given other rectangle intersects with this rectangle.
---@param rect Rect The rectangle to test.
---@return boolean # Whether the given rectangle intersects with this rectangle.
function Rect:Intersects(rect) end

---Returns a rectangle which covers where the given rectangle and this rectangle intersect.
---
---If there is no intersection, then `nil` is returned.
---@param rect Rect The rectangle to intersect with.
---@return Rect? # The intersection rectangle. Returns `nil` if there is no intersection.
function Rect:GetIntersection(rect) end

---Returns a rectangle which encompasses both the given rectangle and this rectangle.
---@param rect Rect The rectangle to union with.
---@return Rect # The encompassing rectangle.
---@overload fun(self: Rect, x: number, y: number): Rect
function Rect:GetUnion(rect) end
